<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Air-defence gate profile. Mirrors gating.py:_defender_predicates EXACTLY.

  Hand over to the policy exactly when the scripted law ITSELF is in its
  gate-point fallback (GuardDefenders::plan sets `scripted_fallback`: no
  intercept for its assigned threat). Read off the law, not approximated.

  1. Not the tag heuristic. One predicate at a time on the original law
     (assault, 150 eps x 2 blocks): scripted 0.54/0.56; InterceptInfeasible->rl
     0.70/0.71; + ThreatImminent 0.45; + DefenderCloseQuarters 0.12. "Close
     quarters is messy, hand it over" costs 42 points in air defence.

  2. The old InterceptInfeasible was a proxy (point solve, NEAREST threat) that
     disagreed with the law's own switch on 37% of its fallback ticks, and the
     point solve ignored the 1.4 m capture radius. With the law solving against
     a 0.7 m sphere and this tree reading its own flag (held-out seeds 20000+,
     n=200, paired), defender win rate:
                                         assault   escort
         old scripted + old gate ....... 0.730     0.495   (previously shipped)
         sphere scripted ............... 0.795     0.545
         sphere scripted + this tree ... 0.845     0.620   <- shipped
     Over the fixed law the old proxy LOSES (-0.13 assault): it hands over
     geometry the law now handles. InterceptInfeasible, ThreatImminent and
     DefenderCloseQuarters stay registered in bt_nodes.cpp so every row above
     reproduces from Groot2 by editing this file alone.

  3. The handover is IMMEDIATE: a k-tick debounce was a dose-response loss
     (0.71/0.59/0.49 for k=1/2/3 at perfect link, nothing recovered under
     latency). Do not re-add one without beating that table.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="GateDefenders">
  <BehaviorTree ID="GateDefenders">
    <Fallback name="gate">
      <Sequence name="scripted_fallback_to_rl">
        <ScriptedFallback/>
        <SetMode mode="rl"/>
      </Sequence>
      <Sequence name="clean_intercept_to_scripted">
        <CleanInterceptScripted/>
        <SetMode mode="scripted"/>
      </Sequence>
      <SetMode mode="scripted"/>
    </Fallback>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
